---
slug: forgot-password
method: post
layout: dashboard_account
searchable: false
metadata: {
    "page_name": "Forgot Password - Submit",
    "page_title": "Forgot Password | Seedling",
    "meta_title": "Forgot Password",
    "is_visible_to_search_engines": false,
    "is_sitemap_enabled": false
}
---

{%- liquid
  if context.current_user
    redirect_to '/dashboard'
    break
  endif

  comment
    A post without a valid authenticity token is not refused: it arrives with an empty
    session. The forgot-password page sets this flag, so its absence means the token was
    missing or wrong.
  endcomment
  if context.session.forgot_password_form != 'on'
    redirect_to '/forgot-password?error=session'
    break
  endif

  assign email = context.params.email | default: '' | append: '' | strip | downcase
  assign email_ok = false
  if email != blank
    assign email_ok = email | is_email_valid
  endif
  unless email_ok
    response_status 422
    render 'account/forgot_password_form', email: email, error: 'invalid'
    break
  endunless

  comment
    An instance with no sendable sender (see emails/sender) cannot send, so say so rather
    than promise an email.
  endcomment
  function sender = 'emails/sender'
  unless sender.ok
    response_status 503
    render 'account/forgot_password_form', email: email, error: 'unavailable'
    break
  endunless

  comment
    5 requests per address and 20 per IP address in 15 minutes. Past the limit nothing is
    sent, and the answer is the same as for a real request, so the limit does not tell
    anyone whether the address has an account.
  endcomment
  function allowed = 'account/rate_limit/allow', action: 'forgot_password', key: email, max_per_key: 5, max_per_ip: 20
  if allowed
    comment
      Saving the token through the update_password_token form sends the forgot_password
      email. An address with no account finds no user, so nothing is saved or sent.
    endcomment
    graphql generated = 'account/generate_user_temporary_token', email: email
    assign user = generated.items.results | first
    if user.id != blank
      graphql saved = 'account/update_password_token', id: user.id, token: user.temporary_token
    endif
  endif

  redirect_to '/forgot-password?sent=1'
-%}
